      "message": "fix(post): built-in VMC and tilt-head stroke bands in program coordinates\n\nThe VMC 3-axis (vmc.mch) and tilt-head (tilthead.mch) stated their\nmachine-frame strokes (Z -500..0, X +/-300, Y +/-250), but the limit\nchecker reads travel in program coordinates through the work offset.\nEvery move above the Z0 work origin - every retract and clearance -\nwas out of stroke, so no program posted on the built-in VMC.\n\nRestate both files the way the Tormach files already are: a stroke L\nis -L..L (the work origin may sit anywhere along the slide). Z is now\n-500..500, X -600..600, Y -500..500. The rule is spelled out in the\napp::machine module doc and assets/machines/AGENTS.md. A program that\nreaches past L from its own origin still refuses by name.\n\nPinned by vmc_stroke: a plate contour on the built-in VMC passes the\ngate and posts; a Z 520 clearance is refused naming Z and the stroke.\n\nFixes #457\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
